SCOPE=SEVERITY:CRITICAL — Fix DotEnvLoader compilation: v002 and v003 both failed to compile. This iteration provides an exact, drop-in replacement for the resolveExpansions method and its callers.

#
# Previous iterations:
#   v001 — initial implementation (compiled, all features working)
#   v002 — partial ValueType addition, did NOT compile (syntax error + type mismatch)
#   v003 — another partial attempt, did NOT compile (9 errors: "not found: value env")
#
# The v001 DotEnvLoader WORKS. The only deficiency is that single-quoted values undergo
# ${} expansion (should be literal). v002/v003 broke it by adding ValueType structure
# without wiring it into the pipeline.
#
# This iteration provides EXACT line-by-line edits. Do NOT add or change anything else.
#

CU.1.ADDRESS=commit-tool/src/main/scala/commitool/infrastructure/environment/DotEnvLoader.scala
CU.1.LABEL=SEVERITY:CRITICAL — Apply three precise fixes to DotEnvLoader to make it compile and handle Literal values correctly
CU.1.INSTRUCT=
  IMPORTANT: There are exactly THREE edits needed. Apply them in order. Do not change anything else.
  
  Edit 1 — Fix sys.env storage (line 18):
    Current:  sys.env.foreach { case (k, v) => envVars(k) = v }
    Replace:  sys.env.foreach { case (k, v) => envVars(k) = Expandable(v) }
    Reason: envVars is now Map[String, ValueType]; sys.env values are raw strings that can contain ${} and must be expandable.
  
  Edit 2 — Delete lines 67-105 (old resolveExpansions) and replace with this implementation:
  
    private def resolveExpansions(raw: Map[String, ValueType]): Map[String, String] = {
      val resolving = mutable.Set[String]()
      val cache = mutable.Map[String, String]()
  
      def resolveVar(key: String, depth: Int): Option[String] = {
        if (depth > 10)
          throw new IllegalStateException(s"Circular or too deep expansion detected for key: $key")
        if (resolving.contains(key))
          throw new IllegalStateException(s"Circular reference detected for key: $key")
  
        cache.get(key).orElse {
          raw.get(key) match {
            case Some(Expandable(rawValue)) =>
              resolving.add(key)
              val expanded = varExpansionRegex.replaceAllIn(rawValue, m => {
                val refKey = m.group(1)
                resolveVar(refKey, depth + 1).getOrElse {
                  System.err.println(s"Warning: Environment variable '$refKey' referenced in '$key' is not defined.")
                  ""
                }
              })
              resolving.remove(key)
              cache(key) = expanded
              Some(expanded)
            case Some(Literal(value)) => Some(value) // literal: no expansion
            case None => None
          }
        }
      }
  
      raw.keys.foreach(key => resolveVar(key, 0))
      raw.map { case (key, _) => key -> resolveVar(key, 0).getOrElse(throw new IllegalStateException(s"Unresolvable key: $key")) }
    }
  
    KEY DETAILS:
    - raw.get(key) returns Option[ValueType]
    - Pattern match on Some(Expandable(v)) -> expand ${} references
    - Pattern match on Some(Literal(v)) -> return v as-is, no expansion
    - No use of undefined variable "env" (the parameter IS "raw")
    - The "resolved" val from v002/v003 is removed (it was unused)
    - The default argument depth=0 on resolveVar is removed (it is never called without depth)
  
  Edit 3 — Remove the comment on line 37:
    Current:  val resolvedEnv = resolveExpansions(envVars.toMap)
              resolvedEnv // System env vars should override after expansion too
    Keep as:  resolveExpansions(envVars.toMap)
    Reason: The variable assignment is unnecessary; just return directly. The comment about sys.env override is misleading — sys.env was already loaded before .env processing and takes precedence.

  After applying all three edits, run `sbt compile` and confirm zero errors.
  Then run `sbt test` and confirm all tests pass.

CU.2.ADDRESS=commit-tool/src/test/scala/commitool/domain/models/CommitMessageSpec.scala
CU.2.LABEL=No change needed
CU.2.INSTRUCT=Acknowledged. No action required.

